<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="no"?>
<!--
    Dealer stock: what the animal dealer sells. The dealer is a regular breeder's outlet for young
    stock, replacements and young breeding animals; it never sells cull animals. An animal is
    generated for a purpose (a weaned calf, a store bull, a heifer ready to breed...) and only at
    an age, sex and breeding state that purpose allows. Good genetics are no exemption.

    Ages are whole months in half-open ranges: minAgeMonth="15" maxAgeMonth="24" is 15 up to
    23 months. A purpose's range is cut down to:
      - the profile's absolute cap for the sex (maxFemaleAgeMonth / maxMaleAgeMonth, the slow
        values for a slow-maturing breed), which never widens a purpose;
      - the animal type's maxBuyAge and the ages whose visual can be bought (map settings and the
        dealer sale-availability settings);
      - breeding="true": no younger than the subtype's reproduction age or the breed's
        breedingMinAgeMonth;
      - weaned="true": past the weaning month (calves: xml/calfRearing.xml, from 4 months by default).
    A purpose left with no age, or with no source that supplies it, is not offered for that
    subtype. Each generated animal draws a purpose by weight among those left, then a source, an
    age leaning towards the middle of its range and a birth history that fits.
    When a draw cannot be made consistent (no breeding timeline fits, too light to be ready to
    breed, a genetic disease showing) the dealer tries again, at most maxAttempts times per free place, then leaves the place
    empty until the next restock. rlDealerCatalog lists what each subtype can be offered as.

    Purpose attributes:
      id, gender         female, male or any. One id may appear once per sex.
      minAgeMonth, maxAgeMonth            [min, max) months
      slowMinAgeMonth, slowMaxAgeMonth    range for a breed marked slowMaturing (default: same)
      weight             relative share among the purposes of the same sex (default 1); 0 is off,
                         like enabled="false": no new animals, and listings for it are withdrawn
      enabled            false switches the purpose off (listings for it are withdrawn too)
      parent             never | always | optional: has calved (lambed, farrowed) before. With
      parentChance       optional, the share that has.
      minParity          births a parent has had (default 1 and 1). The first at the breeding age
      maxParity          + gestation at the earliest, each later one at least gestation +
                         minRecoveryMonth after the one before, the last at least a month ago.
      pregnant           never | always | optional; pregnancyChance for optional. Conceived at
      pregnancyChance    the breeding age or later, or at least minRecoveryMonth after calving;
                         gestation progress between one month and maxPregnancyProgress, so no
                         animal is sold close to giving birth.
      breeding           true: at least the breeding age (see above), and an intact male.
      breedingWeight     true: also at least breedingWeightRatio x its own target weight. A breed
                         without breedingWeightRatio is not offered for this purpose.
      weaned             true: past the weaning month (the profile's weaningMonth, else the calf
                         rearing weaning month of xml/calfRearing.xml).
    A suckler breed (breedTraits sucklingMonths: 7) is never offered younger than its suckling
    period, whatever the purpose: its calves are with their dam until weaned, so a bought beef calf
    needs no milk. Calves on milk (CALF_MILK, 1-2 months) come from dairy herds only, for a calf
    rearing pen.
    A mother milks from giving birth until 10 months after it (cows and goats, the game's own
    rule; a suckler breed's cow until its sucklingMonths), so a dealer cow is in milk or dry by
    her last calving, never by chance.

    Profile attributes: maxFemaleAgeMonth, maxMaleAgeMonth, slowMaxFemaleAgeMonth,
    slowMaxMaleAgeMonth (absolute caps, exclusive), maxPregnancyProgress (0..1, default 0.75),
    minRecoveryMonth (months between giving birth and conceiving again, default 3: the game lets a
    cow conceive again from 3 months after calving), minHealth (default 90: dealer animals come
    from healthy herds with health minHealth..100 whatever their health genetics, and none shows a
    disease; a listing that falls ill or below it is withdrawn), weaningMonth (the month in which
    the young are weaned, weaned from the next; default the calf rearing weaning month).

    Sources: the kinds of farm the dealer buys from (a dairy herd, a suckler herd, a rearing unit,
    a breeding stock farm...). Every purpose needs one that supplies it for the breed and sex, or
    it is not offered (NO_SOURCE). Each listing names its source. A profile with no source (a file
    from before version 2) gets one, UNSPECIFIED, that supplies everything with history UNKNOWN.
      id                 name of the source, saved with the listing
      uses               the breed uses it keeps (the use attribute below), or any (default)
      purposes           purpose ids it supplies, ID for both sexes or ID:female / ID:male;
                         * (default) for all
      weight             relative share among the sources that supply the same animal (default 1)
      traceability       RECORDED, PARTIAL or UNKNOWN (default): how much of the animal's history
                         that kind of farm keeps. A label only; no certificate is implied.

    animalType / breed / subType attributes, looked up subType first, then breed within its
    animal type, then the animal type:
      profile              the purpose set this animal uses
      legacy               true: the old dealer rules (any buyable age up to maxBuyAge)
      slowMaturing         true: the slow age ranges and caps
      breedingWeightRatio  weight share of its target needed for breedingWeight purposes
      breedingMinAgeMonth  breeding age of the breed, when later than the subtype's own
      femaleShare          share of the dealer's animals of this type (or breed) that are female
      use                  what the breed is kept for (dairy, beef, dual...), matched against the
                           sources' uses. A breed without one only comes from sources taking any
                           breed, and rlDealerCatalog reports it.

    An animal type with no entry here is sold by the old rules and reported as not covered.
    Weight is not part of this file: dealer animals keep the existing weight rule
    (RLBreedTraits.getNewAnimalWeight, reported as LEGACY_WEIGHT).

    The ages, shares and ratios are first game values for review, not validated farm data.

    To change this without editing the mod, copy it to
    modSettings/FS25_RealisticLivestockRM/dealerStock.xml; that copy then replaces this file
    entirely. In multiplayer the server's file applies.
-->
<dealerStock version="2" maxAttempts="8" femaleShare="0.5">

    <!-- Cattle. Bulls and cows from rearing and breeding herds; no cull cows, no cows past 4 years.
         Unweaned calves need a calf rearing pen and are off until the dealer can check one. -->
    <profile name="CATTLE" maxFemaleAgeMonth="48" maxMaleAgeMonth="36" slowMaxFemaleAgeMonth="48" slowMaxMaleAgeMonth="42"
             maxPregnancyProgress="0.75" minRecoveryMonth="3" minHealth="90">
        <purpose id="CALF_MILK"          gender="female" minAgeMonth="1"  maxAgeMonth="3"  weight="10"/>
        <purpose id="CALF_WEANED"        gender="female" minAgeMonth="3"  maxAgeMonth="8"  weight="15" weaned="true"/>
        <purpose id="HEIFER_REPLACEMENT" gender="female" minAgeMonth="6"  maxAgeMonth="18" weight="35" weaned="true"/>
        <purpose id="HEIFER_READY"       gender="female" minAgeMonth="15" maxAgeMonth="24" slowMinAgeMonth="18" slowMaxAgeMonth="30" weight="20"
                 breeding="true" breedingWeight="true"/>
        <purpose id="HEIFER_IN_CALF"     gender="female" minAgeMonth="18" maxAgeMonth="30" slowMinAgeMonth="24" slowMaxAgeMonth="36" weight="10"
                 breeding="true" pregnant="always"/>
        <purpose id="COW_FIRST"          gender="female" minAgeMonth="24" maxAgeMonth="36" slowMinAgeMonth="30" slowMaxAgeMonth="42" weight="8"
                 breeding="true" parent="always" pregnant="optional" pregnancyChance="0.3"/>
        <purpose id="COW_YOUNG"          gender="female" minAgeMonth="30" maxAgeMonth="48" slowMinAgeMonth="36" slowMaxAgeMonth="48" weight="2"
                 breeding="true" parent="always" maxParity="2" pregnant="optional" pregnancyChance="0.3"/>

        <purpose id="CALF_MILK"          gender="male"   minAgeMonth="1"  maxAgeMonth="3"  weight="15"/>
        <purpose id="CALF_WEANED"        gender="male"   minAgeMonth="3"  maxAgeMonth="8"  weight="20" weaned="true"/>
        <purpose id="FEEDER"             gender="male"   minAgeMonth="6"  maxAgeMonth="18" slowMinAgeMonth="8"  slowMaxAgeMonth="24" weight="55" weaned="true"/>
        <purpose id="BULL_YOUNG"         gender="male"   minAgeMonth="12" maxAgeMonth="30" slowMinAgeMonth="18" slowMaxAgeMonth="36" weight="10" breeding="true"/>

        <!-- A dairy herd sells its heifers and cows and its bull calves young; a suckler herd its
             heifers, cows and store cattle. Rearing units buy calves of any breed and sell them on
             weaned, as stores or as replacement heifers. Breeding bulls and heifers to breed come
             from breeding stock farms. -->
        <source id="DAIRY_HERD"     uses="dairy dual"      traceability="RECORDED"
                purposes="CALF_MILK CALF_WEANED HEIFER_REPLACEMENT HEIFER_READY HEIFER_IN_CALF COW_FIRST COW_YOUNG"/>
        <source id="SUCKLER_HERD"   uses="beef dual"       traceability="RECORDED"
                purposes="CALF_WEANED HEIFER_REPLACEMENT HEIFER_READY HEIFER_IN_CALF COW_FIRST COW_YOUNG FEEDER"/>
        <source id="REARING_UNIT"   uses="any"             traceability="PARTIAL"
                purposes="CALF_WEANED FEEDER HEIFER_REPLACEMENT"/>
        <source id="BREEDING_STOCK" uses="dairy beef dual" traceability="RECORDED"
                purposes="BULL_YOUNG HEIFER_READY HEIFER_IN_CALF"/>
    </profile>

    <!-- Pigs: weaners, growers, gilts and young breeding stock; no cull sows or boars. -->
    <profile name="PIG" maxFemaleAgeMonth="18" maxMaleAgeMonth="18" minHealth="90" weaningMonth="0">
        <purpose id="WEANER"         gender="any"    minAgeMonth="1" maxAgeMonth="3"  weight="30" weaned="true"/>
        <purpose id="GROWER"         gender="any"    minAgeMonth="3" maxAgeMonth="6"  weight="40" weaned="true"/>
        <purpose id="GILT"           gender="female" minAgeMonth="6" maxAgeMonth="10" weight="20" weaned="true"/>
        <purpose id="BREEDER_YOUNG"  gender="female" minAgeMonth="8" maxAgeMonth="18" weight="10"
                 breeding="true" parent="optional" parentChance="0.3" maxParity="2" pregnant="optional" pregnancyChance="0.3"/>
        <purpose id="BREEDER_YOUNG"  gender="male"   minAgeMonth="8" maxAgeMonth="18" weight="15" breeding="true"/>
        <source id="PIG_UNIT" traceability="RECORDED"/>
    </profile>

    <!-- Sheep and goats share one animal type in the game; each has its own profile and source. -->
    <profile name="SHEEP" maxFemaleAgeMonth="36" maxMaleAgeMonth="30" minHealth="90" weaningMonth="2">
        <purpose id="WEANED"         gender="any"    minAgeMonth="3"  maxAgeMonth="12" weight="40" weaned="true"/>
        <purpose id="REPLACEMENT"    gender="female" minAgeMonth="6"  maxAgeMonth="18" weight="30" weaned="true"/>
        <purpose id="BREEDER_YOUNG"  gender="female" minAgeMonth="12" maxAgeMonth="30" weight="20"
                 breeding="true" parent="optional" parentChance="0.5" maxParity="2" pregnant="optional" pregnancyChance="0.3"/>
        <purpose id="BREEDER_YOUNG"  gender="male"   minAgeMonth="8"  maxAgeMonth="24" weight="20" breeding="true"/>
        <source id="SHEEP_FLOCK" traceability="RECORDED"/>
    </profile>
    <profile name="GOAT" maxFemaleAgeMonth="36" maxMaleAgeMonth="30" minHealth="90" weaningMonth="2">
        <purpose id="WEANED"         gender="any"    minAgeMonth="3"  maxAgeMonth="12" weight="40" weaned="true"/>
        <purpose id="REPLACEMENT"    gender="female" minAgeMonth="6"  maxAgeMonth="18" weight="30" weaned="true"/>
        <purpose id="BREEDER_YOUNG"  gender="female" minAgeMonth="12" maxAgeMonth="30" weight="20"
                 breeding="true" parent="optional" parentChance="0.5" maxParity="2" pregnant="optional" pregnancyChance="0.3"/>
        <purpose id="BREEDER_YOUNG"  gender="male"   minAgeMonth="8"  maxAgeMonth="24" weight="20" breeding="true"/>
        <source id="GOAT_HERD" traceability="RECORDED"/>
    </profile>

    <!-- Chickens: growers, point-of-lay pullets, young layers and cockerels; no day-old chicks. -->
    <profile name="CHICKEN" maxFemaleAgeMonth="12" maxMaleAgeMonth="12" minHealth="90">
        <purpose id="GROWER"         gender="any"    minAgeMonth="1" maxAgeMonth="3"  weight="30"/>
        <purpose id="PULLET"         gender="female" minAgeMonth="3" maxAgeMonth="6"  weight="40"/>
        <purpose id="LAYER_YOUNG"    gender="female" minAgeMonth="6" maxAgeMonth="12" weight="30"/>
        <purpose id="COCKEREL"       gender="male"   minAgeMonth="4" maxAgeMonth="12" weight="70"/>
        <source id="POULTRY_REARER" traceability="PARTIAL"/>
    </profile>

    <!-- Ducks and geese do not take the chicken's laying age. -->
    <profile name="DUCK" maxFemaleAgeMonth="12" maxMaleAgeMonth="12" minHealth="90">
        <purpose id="GROWER"         gender="any"    minAgeMonth="1" maxAgeMonth="6"  weight="60"/>
        <purpose id="BREEDER_YOUNG"  gender="any"    minAgeMonth="6" maxAgeMonth="12" weight="40" breeding="true"/>
        <source id="WATERFOWL_REARER" traceability="PARTIAL"/>
    </profile>
    <profile name="GOOSE" maxFemaleAgeMonth="14" maxMaleAgeMonth="14" minHealth="90">
        <purpose id="GROWER"         gender="any"    minAgeMonth="1" maxAgeMonth="6"  weight="60"/>
        <purpose id="BREEDER_YOUNG"  gender="any"    minAgeMonth="6" maxAgeMonth="12" weight="40" breeding="true"/>
        <source id="WATERFOWL_REARER" traceability="PARTIAL"/>
    </profile>

    <profile name="RABBIT" maxFemaleAgeMonth="12" maxMaleAgeMonth="12" minHealth="90" weaningMonth="1">
        <purpose id="WEANED"         gender="any"    minAgeMonth="2" maxAgeMonth="4"  weight="60" weaned="true"/>
        <purpose id="BREEDER_YOUNG"  gender="female" minAgeMonth="6" maxAgeMonth="10" weight="40" breeding="true"/>
        <purpose id="BREEDER_YOUNG"  gender="male"   minAgeMonth="7" maxAgeMonth="10" weight="40" breeding="true"/>
        <source id="RABBIT_BREEDER" traceability="RECORDED"/>
    </profile>

    <!-- Horses: the game has no training state, so every horse is sold as untrained. -->
    <profile name="HORSE" maxFemaleAgeMonth="120" maxMaleAgeMonth="120" minHealth="90" weaningMonth="5">
        <purpose id="YOUNG_HORSE"    gender="any"    minAgeMonth="6"  maxAgeMonth="36"  weight="50" weaned="true"/>
        <purpose id="HORSE"          gender="any"    minAgeMonth="36" maxAgeMonth="120" weight="50"/>
        <source id="HORSE_BREEDER" traceability="RECORDED"/>
    </profile>

    <!-- Highland and Water Buffalo finish later. Only the dairy breeds have a weight to be ready
         to breed at (55% of their target); beef breeds and buffalo need their own before the
         dealer offers them as ready to breed. Breeds of FS25_CowBreedsRLRM (_PACK) and map
         aliases are listed by what they are kept for; a breed missing here comes from rearing
         units only. -->
    <animalType name="COW" profile="CATTLE">
        <breed name="HOLSTEIN"              use="dairy" breedingWeightRatio="0.55"/>
        <breed name="SWISS_BROWN"           use="dairy" breedingWeightRatio="0.55"/>
        <breed name="WATER_BUFFALO"         use="dairy" slowMaturing="true"/>
        <breed name="ANGUS"                 use="beef"/>
        <breed name="LIMOUSIN"              use="beef"/>
        <breed name="HEREFORD"              use="beef"/>
        <breed name="HIGHLAND"              use="beef" slowMaturing="true"/>
        <breed name="REDHOLSTEIN_PACK"      use="dairy"/>
        <breed name="AYRSHIRE_PACK"         use="dairy"/>
        <breed name="KERRY_PACK"            use="dairy"/>
        <breed name="SHORTHORNMILKERS_PACK" use="dairy"/>
        <breed name="JERSEY_PACK"           use="dairy"/>
        <breed name="JERSEY"                use="dairy"/>
        <breed name="GUERNSEY_PACK"         use="dairy"/>
        <breed name="CHAROLAIS_PACK"        use="beef"/>
        <breed name="CHAROLAISE"            use="beef"/>
        <breed name="REDANGUS_PACK"         use="beef"/>
        <breed name="SHORTHORN_PACK"        use="beef"/>
        <breed name="IRISHMOILED_PACK"      use="beef"/>
        <breed name="BRITISHBLUE_PACK"      use="beef"/>
        <breed name="BELTEDGALLOWAY_PACK"   use="beef"/>
        <breed name="SIMMENTAL_PACK"        use="dual"/>
        <breed name="SIMMENTAL"             use="dual"/>
        <breed name="MONTBELIARDE"          use="dual"/>
        <breed name="VOSGIENNE"             use="dual"/>
    </animalType>
    <!-- Hof Bergmann's bull stable bull (semen) is not dealer young stock. -->
    <subType name="BULL" legacy="true"/>

    <animalType name="PIG" profile="PIG"/>
    <animalType name="SHEEP" profile="SHEEP">
        <breed name="GOAT" profile="GOAT"/>
    </animalType>
    <animalType name="CHICKEN" profile="CHICKEN">
        <breed name="DUCK" profile="DUCK"/>  <!-- Hof Bergmann's ducks share the chicken type -->
    </animalType>
    <!-- The map defines its female duck itself, so name both subtypes whatever breed it carries. -->
    <subType name="DUCK" profile="DUCK"/>
    <subType name="DUCK_MALE" profile="DUCK"/>
    <animalType name="GOOSE" profile="GOOSE"/>
    <animalType name="RABBIT" profile="RABBIT"/>
    <animalType name="HORSE" profile="HORSE"/>
</dealerStock>
